.TH "zelta\-rebase" "8" "" "" "System Manager\(cqs Manual"
.SH NAME
\f[B]zelta rebase\f[R] \- build a new dataset tree from an upgraded
upstream while preserving backup continuity
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]zelta rebase\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] \f[I]origin\f[R]
\f[I]target\f[R] \f[I]upstream\f[R] [\f[I]new\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]zelta rebase\f[R] composes a replication workflow for replacing a
production tree with a new tree based on an upgraded upstream while
preserving incremental backup continuity through an existing origin
backup.
.PP
This is useful for image, template, appliance, and development workflows
where local changes must move forward onto a newer upstream base without
forcing a full backup history restart.
.PP
The workflow uses existing ZFS lineage information and Zelta backup
state.
It is not a destructive overwrite workflow; divergent datasets are
preserved according to Zelta\(cqs normal safety model.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[I]origin\f[R]
Existing origin backup or lineage member used as the continuity basis.
.TP
\f[I]target\f[R]
Current production or working dataset tree to be rebased.
.TP
\f[I]upstream\f[R]
Upgraded upstream dataset tree.
.TP
\f[I]new\f[R]
Optional destination for the newly composed dataset tree.
.TP
\f[B]\-n\f[R], \f[B]\-\-dryrun\f[R], \f[B]\-\-dry\-run\f[R]
Display underlying commands without executing them.
.TP
\f[B]\-v\f[R], \f[B]\-\-verbose\f[R]
Increase verbosity.
Specify once for operational detail, twice for debug output.
.TP
\f[B]\-q\f[R], \f[B]\-\-quiet\f[R]
Decrease log output.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compose a rebased tree from an upgraded upstream:
.IP
.EX
zelta rebase backup:tank/origin tank/app upstream:tank/app\-v2 tank/app\-v2
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, non\-zero on error.
.SH NOTES
Use \f[B]zelta match\f[R] before and after rebasing to confirm lineage
and backup state.
